Specs of the PyQt GUIs other than control_gui, one per file that constructs a QApplication (qapps.py).
check_gui_parity.py reads them; see its docstring and ../../README.md ("Parity with the other PyQt GUIs").

  <name>.json         {"file", "web", "backend", "walk": {...}, "mapping": {...}}  or  {"file", "na", "rule"}
  <name>.walk.json    the offscreen walk of that GUI against the simulated DAQ (qt_walk --gui), saved by
                      check_gui_parity --run-walks --sim-daq <daq_sim work dir>; the check refuses a walk of
                      other source (sha256 of the GUI's own files)
  <name>.probe.json   qt_walk --probe-import result (rule library-demo)

Mapping entries: {"web": "[data-parity~=\"<row id>\"]", "test": "test_gui_<name>.py::<test>[chromium]"} or
{"na": "<one-line reason citing the guard>"}.  The tests list their rows in PARITY_ROWS (conftest records them).
